<title>USA: U.S. MTBE REMAINS FIRM ON TIGHT SUPPLY.</title>
<headline>U.S. MTBE REMAINS FIRM ON TIGHT SUPPLY.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cents/Gallon  Prompt(Aug)   Any (Aug)	08/06/97(PptAug)</p>
<p>Houston     94.50/95.00	94.50/94.50	  94.50/95.00</p>
<p>New York   101.00/102.00     99.00/100.00N   101.00/102.00</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>U.S. spot MTBE prices remained strong Friday morning amid some refiner demand and continued tight supply of MTBE and octanes.</p>
<p>In the U.S. Gulf, prompt MTBE was bought by refiner for 95.00 cents for 50,000 barrels late Thursday, about a quarter cent above Wednesday.</p>
<p>A New York Harbor parcel was also bought Thursday by a refiner for 101.00 cents. Friday's range was talked 101.00/102.00 cents.</p>
<p>-- Laney Salisbury, New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1631--</p>
